// REJECTS: Unexpected token 'property'. Valid alternatives: ['points', 'source', 'target']
//
// The three view kinds have DIFFERENT field sets, and unlike the required/only-once rules
// this one is in the grammar. A generalizationView takes source, target and points; a
// propertyView takes those plus `property`, which is what identifies the edge.
//
// The alternatives list enumerates the whole legal set, which makes this the cheapest
// possible pin on view-kind field partitioning. A rewrite that parses "a view is a name,
// a brace block, and a bag of colon-terminated fields" -- an entirely reasonable shape,
// since classView, propertyView and generalizationView look identical from the outside --
// accepts a property on a generalization edge and emits protocol with a dangling reference.
###Diagram
Diagram fixture::neg::GenWithProperty
{
   generalizationView
   {
      property: fixture::neg::Person.firm;
      source: a;
      target: b;
      points: [];
   }
}
